  appearance coming in one division and  her response was  yes so that means whoever this cameo is  that both elizabeth olsen and paul  bettany are talking about  is a really really big cameo and luke  skywalker was somebody that was from the  original star wars films  which leads many people to believe  including myself that they're going to  bring an  old marvel actor back to reprise a role  and now  after one division episode 5 where they  brought back quicksilver  not aaron taylor johnson's quicksilver  but evan peters quicksilver from the  other marvel x-men universe anything is  freaking possible with marvel  but let's dissect a few parts of the  last episode of wanda vision  now for those of you who may not know at  one point in time in the comics magneto  was retconned to be  the father of quicksilver and the  scarlet witch  so wanda and pietro's father was magneto  specifically he was their father during  the house of  m story which we already know is a heavy  influence on what we're seeing  in one division now what's really  interesting about this is that in the  house of m storyline  quicksilver dies but wanda resurrects  him she brings him back to life  and she does this by warping reality  something that we are seeing  right now in one division and it does  look like she revived her brother  in this alternate reality now i kind of  think he's evil and think maybe she  didn't actually revive him but still  he's revived which goes along with the  house of m storyline now of course the  biggest part of quicksilver appearing at  the end of one division episode 5  is that it's not aaron taylor johnson's  quicksilver who is the mcu  quicksilver that we saw on avengers age  of ultron it's evan peters's quicksilver  from the fox universe from the x-men  movies  now this was insanely awesome but it has  a lot of fans wondering exactly what the  heck is going on  is he actually quicksilver from that  x-men universe we know that one division  leads up to doctor strange and the  multiverse of madness and the multiverse  is going to be a huge factor moving  forward now as far as magneto was  concerned the fact that they resurrected  this quicksilver  actually makes a lot of sense because in  the fox universe in the x-men films  this quicksilver finds out that magneto  is his father  so that's the route that fox went they  went the route of magneto  being the father of wanda and pietro and  now seemingly  that quicksilver whose father was  magneto is in the mcu  and is the brother of r wanda could they  be doing a type of retcon to where  wanda is the daughter of magneto kevin  feige has officially announced that the  mutants are coming to the mcu  and technically quicksilver is the first  mutant to enter the mcu  but it wouldn't be surprising if mutants  started to show up randomly  now in this episode of one division it  did reveal who their parents were it  said their names but that happens in the  comics too  they believed their parents to be the  maximoffs but in reality magneto was  their father  so that could be the same thing in one  division and if you look closely at some  scenes there are a lot of resemblances  between the x-men and one division and  wanda and  magneto in the epic scene where wanda  walks out of her reality with the drone  and throws it back at sword  wanda would soon after turn all the  sword agents on tyler hayward  right before she does this she says i'm  not the one with the guns  this seems to be a mirror scene from the  original x-men film in 2000 where  magneto used his ability to control  metal to turn the soldiers guns against  themselves  as he drops the line you homo sapiens  and your guns and that was sir ian  mckellen's magneto  but it also mirrors a scene from michael  fassbender's magneto from 2019's dark  phoenix the scene on the train where he  uses his powers to take control of the  weaponry on board the train  but perhaps the most direct connection  between wanda and magneto comes 